Subject: [BioC] DESeq nbinomGLMTest specific comparisons
In-Reply-To: <CEF4384A.19FC%j.a.floyd@qmul.ac.uk>
References: <CEBA7B20.154C%j.a.floyd@qmul.ac.uk>
	<CAHA9McOMOku1XhRoudB_Z_4qnNjzhO5BdejMnmR8nRnD6uou_Q@mail.gmail.com>
	<CEF4384A.19FC%j.a.floyd@qmul.ac.uk>
Message-ID: <52D02B73.7020705@thompsonclan.org>

In general, you would subset the CountDataSet to only include the 
samples from the two conditions you care about. Do this after 
estimating dispersions and before fitNbinomGLMs.

But more generally, I agree that the real solution is "use DESeq2".

-Ryan

