Subject: [BioC] edgeR  FC calculation question
In-Reply-To: <2639CB5887B7B844A85E581C733BA684E82A11EB23@EXCH-CCR01.lj.ad.scripps.edu>
References: <2639CB5887B7B844A85E581C733BA684E82A11EB23@EXCH-CCR01.lj.ad.scripps.edu>
Message-ID: <52D9A4D5.60703@thompsonclan.org>

Hi Lana,

The fold change (actually log2 fold change) for a contrast is simply 
the sum/difference of all the coefficients in the contrast as you have 
written it. So if Drug.1h, Drug.0h, Placebo.1h, and Placebo.0h are 4 
coefficients in your model, then your "DrugvsPlacebo.1h" contrast works 
out to:

1 * Drug.1h + -1 * Drug.0h + -1 * Placebo.1h + 1 * Placebo.0h

The logFC for each gene is computed by substituting the fitted values 
for each coefficient into the expression that you specify as the 
contrast.

-Ryan

